WEBVTT

00:00.890 --> 00:03.480
Otonashi Sumi-san's death was no suicide.

00:05.060 --> 00:07.520
Now, let me tell you who the real killer is.

00:08.130 --> 00:09.740
The real killer?

00:15.150 --> 00:17.240
<i>So we've finally made it this far.</i>

01:29.060 --> 01:32.400
I was able to confirm that President 
Otonashi's dealings did indeed take place.

01:32.630 --> 01:34.570
But there's one thing that doesn't sit right.

01:35.660 --> 01:39.380
Fubuki, why didn't you choose 
a way to kill Otonashi Sumi-san

01:39.380 --> 01:42.280
that would look like an illness or accident?

01:42.550 --> 01:45.170
With your powers, as well as 
your ability to transform,

01:45.170 --> 01:46.760
that should have been possible.

01:47.830 --> 01:50.670
You didn't actually kill 
Otonashi Sumi-san, did you?

01:50.980 --> 01:54.370
You acted like you did, reported to Goichi,

01:54.370 --> 01:56.570
and took the prize from your 
agreement anyway, didn't you?

01:59.270 --> 02:00.970
As perceptive as ever...

02:02.040 --> 02:03.560
My lady.

02:06.220 --> 02:09.730
I did not kill that woman.

02:09.980 --> 02:14.440
But I didn't intend to deceive that human 
named Goichi from the start, either.

02:14.730 --> 02:19.700
That night, I had transformed into a stray 
dog so that I could kill that Sumi woman.

02:20.120 --> 02:23.200
I had been targeting that woman 
ever since we'd made our deal,

02:23.200 --> 02:25.950
but that was the first 
time she had been alone.

02:27.450 --> 02:30.010
<i>If I miss this chance, who knows
when the next one will come?</i>

02:30.010 --> 02:31.960
<i>I need to see this through.</i>

02:31.960 --> 02:35.710
My plan was to turn into
a stray dog, attack her,

02:36.100 --> 02:39.720
and rip out her throat in front of 
as many witnesses as possible.

02:39.840 --> 02:44.020
Either that, or I'd chase her into the 
street and have a car run her over.

02:44.600 --> 02:46.770
And yet, would you believe it?

02:46.770 --> 02:48.890
Right before my eyes, that woman

02:48.890 --> 02:52.100
was stabbed to death by a human 
who was waiting to ambush her.

02:52.820 --> 02:57.150
Once the killer confirmed her death, 
they scattered her bag and wallet,

02:57.150 --> 03:00.380
took her money, and fled immediately.

03:01.180 --> 03:03.570
Oh, how could they do such a thing?

03:03.570 --> 03:09.220
Now my deal with that man will 
be ruined. If I don't do something...

03:12.670 --> 03:13.940
Thief!

03:13.940 --> 03:15.580
Someone! That man—

03:15.580 --> 03:19.620
Someone catch that man wearing black! 
He went toward the station!

03:24.610 --> 03:25.960
There's someone on the ground!

03:25.960 --> 03:27.510
Someone call an ambulance!

03:27.510 --> 03:31.520
<b>Goat</b>

03:27.510 --> 03:31.520
So that scream wasn't from 
the victim. It was you.

03:31.520 --> 03:36.020
Yes. That woman was as good as dead 
the moment she was stabbed.

03:36.020 --> 03:39.640
<i>To think that a yoko was involved 
in falsifying what happened...</i>

03:39.640 --> 03:42.530
<i>I guess I'll need to work a little 
harder to have all this make sense.</i>

03:42.780 --> 03:46.830
There was no evidence nor hints left 
at the scene, and no one came forward.

03:46.830 --> 03:48.740
Even though I did not kill the target,

03:48.740 --> 03:50.700
it did not change the fact 
that the target was dead.

03:50.700 --> 03:54.580
Then I figured there was no harm in 
proclaiming that I did what he asked,

03:54.580 --> 03:57.590
so I went to him and told him to 
hold up his end of the bargain.

03:57.590 --> 04:02.270
I did everything I could to make sure his 
family would not be blamed for her death,

04:02.270 --> 04:04.950
so what I asked for was not dishonest.

04:04.950 --> 04:09.270
Meaning you've seen the killer's 
face and know who it is.

04:09.270 --> 04:14.480
And that's why, to protect the killer, 
you purposely screamed out as the victim

04:14.480 --> 04:16.250
so everyone there would hear you.

04:17.100 --> 04:19.230
<i>I see... In that case...</i>

04:19.230 --> 04:23.990
Yes. I had done some research, 
so I knew who the killer was.

04:24.270 --> 04:28.590
And that is why I shouted out 
that the killer was a man.

04:29.590 --> 04:32.380
Which means there's only one 
person who could be the killer.

04:33.110 --> 04:34.740
The killer is...

04:35.250 --> 04:39.940
It's that man's eldest daughter. 
The one named Kaoruko.

04:40.760 --> 04:43.010
The real killer is Kaoruko-san.

04:45.310 --> 04:48.220
It seemed impossible for 
Kaoruko-san to commit the murder,

04:48.220 --> 04:50.030
but as I said yesterday,

04:50.030 --> 04:53.650
it was possible for her to fabricate 
the time that she broke her leg.

04:53.650 --> 04:58.440
She managed to do that successfully, 
and killed Sumi-san.

04:58.780 --> 05:01.570
I want to talk to you about 
my relationship with Koya-san.

05:01.570 --> 05:04.610
This was the only way we could 
talk to each other alone.

05:04.950 --> 05:07.810
Kaoruko-san waited for Sumi-san on the route

05:07.810 --> 05:11.320
from the massage shop to the 
station and approached her.

05:11.320 --> 05:14.350
Sumi-san probably let her approach

05:14.350 --> 05:19.130
since this really was the only way they 
could have one-on-one time together.

05:27.220 --> 05:30.260
In order to make it look like 
a burglary and murder,

05:30.260 --> 05:34.020
Kaoruko-san took Sumi-san's wallet from 
her bag, took just the bills, and fled.

05:35.020 --> 05:38.270
Aunt Kaoruko killed Grandmother?

05:38.550 --> 05:39.400
Koya-san.

05:40.190 --> 05:42.900
You knew of Kaoruko-san's crime, didn't you?

05:43.510 --> 05:46.290
When I saw through the possible 
lie regarding the broken leg,

05:46.290 --> 05:47.670
you didn't try very hard to deny it.

05:47.670 --> 05:49.910
You said it was part of the plan,

05:50.220 --> 05:53.490
but it went wrong. That was brilliant.

05:54.810 --> 05:57.460
From your and Kaoruko-san's positions,

05:57.460 --> 06:02.230
I'm sure this plan by President 
Otonashi must've been terrifying.

06:02.230 --> 06:04.210
The president only meant it to be a way

06:04.210 --> 06:06.260
for all of you to learn of his crimes,

06:06.260 --> 06:09.240
but for you two, it must've 
felt like he was trying

06:09.240 --> 06:12.760
to punish you for your crimes 23 years ago.

06:12.980 --> 06:16.640
Everything out of the president's 
mouth must've sounded like that.

06:17.100 --> 06:18.560
But there was still a possibility

06:18.560 --> 06:21.940
the president proposed this 
task for a different reason.

06:22.290 --> 06:26.070
That's why Koya-san continued to 
simply watch how things unfolded.

06:26.070 --> 06:29.570
But then, Ryoma-san and Susumu-san's 
murder plot came to light,

06:29.890 --> 06:31.660
making everything even more awkward.

06:32.370 --> 06:36.580
And when you realized that I thought 
all of you might be guilty,

06:36.580 --> 06:38.790
you ended up admitting to it.

06:39.010 --> 06:42.720
Because even if the president 
had proof of your plan,

06:42.720 --> 06:45.150
you could still claim it was 
just attempted murder.

06:45.150 --> 06:49.640
By doing so, you were probably trying 
to figure out just how much of the truth

06:49.640 --> 06:51.430
President Otonashi knew, as well.

06:51.670 --> 06:53.860
Eventually, Rion-san came up with a way

06:53.860 --> 06:55.850
President Otonashi could've 
committed the crime.

06:56.150 --> 06:58.840
This is where Koya-san thought 
that President Otonashi

06:58.840 --> 07:01.150
had really carried out what 
Rion-san came up with,

07:01.150 --> 07:02.690
and before that became reality,

07:02.690 --> 07:06.650
he thought he and Kaoruko-san 
had killed Sumi-san.

07:06.980 --> 07:10.220
It's because all three plans were 
coincidentally going on at once

07:10.220 --> 07:12.600
that something so bizarre ended up happening...

07:13.290 --> 07:17.930
That President Otonashi actually 
believed his plan had worked.

07:17.930 --> 07:19.370
That's how you determined that

07:19.640 --> 07:24.380
President Otonashi really was just 
trying to prove his own crime,

07:24.380 --> 07:28.250
putting the two of you at ease last night.

07:28.860 --> 07:32.590
Today, President Otonashi 
admitted his own plan,

07:32.820 --> 07:36.810
and Koya-san was going to just let 
President Otonashi take the fall for it.

07:37.100 --> 07:41.560
If you had interrupted the president 
and come clean with your crimes,

07:41.890 --> 07:48.070
I wouldn't have had to say all this, 
but President Otonashi said...

07:48.070 --> 07:51.850
"Every time you kill someone, 
there is a huge price to pay.

07:51.850 --> 07:54.500
Even if you think everything 
went well after killing someone,

07:54.500 --> 07:56.830
there's still always a 
price to pay in the end."

07:57.170 --> 08:00.410
Since you're staying silent 
even after hearing that,

08:00.410 --> 08:03.180
you're forcing me to speak the truth.

08:03.580 --> 08:06.790
Above all, for President Otonashi's beliefs.

08:09.420 --> 08:12.800
Iwanaga-san, what kind of farce is this?

08:13.060 --> 08:17.550
You yourself disproved the theory that 
Kaoruko was the killer yesterday.

08:17.550 --> 08:20.680
Sumi-san shouted out that 
the killer was a man.

08:20.680 --> 08:24.060
You even proved that the killer didn't 
falsify this information somehow.

08:24.290 --> 08:26.810
Kaoruko is the farthest 
from being the killer.

08:26.810 --> 08:28.890
You and Kaoruko-san were both surprised

08:28.890 --> 08:33.030
to later learn that the victim's 
screams were heard at the scene.

08:33.030 --> 08:35.950
And you knew that put things in your favor.

08:35.950 --> 08:39.970
You might've even thought President 
Otonashi pulled some strings

08:39.970 --> 08:43.960
and fed the police fake information.

08:44.390 --> 08:48.690
And that's why you were scared that 
President Otonashi may have thought

08:48.690 --> 08:50.840
that you were the killers.

08:51.630 --> 08:55.050
Those were actual words that Sumi-san yelled.

08:56.300 --> 08:58.340
In order to protect her daughter,

08:58.340 --> 09:03.480
Sumi-san screamed out with her last breath 
that the person who robbed her was a man.

09:03.730 --> 09:08.120
She tried to protect her own daughter 
from being investigated by the police.

09:09.230 --> 09:11.940
But you debunked that yesterday!

09:12.260 --> 09:13.570
If that was a planned murder,

09:13.970 --> 09:16.450
the killer would've covered 
her mouth when they killed her

09:16.450 --> 09:17.910
to keep others from hearing her.

09:18.190 --> 09:20.440
Furthermore, the killer 
wouldn't have left the scene

09:20.440 --> 09:22.790
until they confirmed she was dead 
and no evidence was left behind!

09:22.790 --> 09:24.040
Koya-san!

09:24.040 --> 09:27.190
If this was a planned murder 
committed by someone she knew,

09:27.190 --> 09:28.920
the victim wouldn't have time to yell.

09:29.330 --> 09:32.180
That's why you came to the conclusion 
that this was an unexpected act

09:32.180 --> 09:34.420
by someone she didn't know!

09:34.420 --> 09:36.240
This was her first murder.

09:36.240 --> 09:39.760
Kaoruko-san wasn't able to 
fully confirm Sumi-san's death.

09:39.760 --> 09:43.220
She decided everything was okay because 
Sumi-san was on the ground and not moving.

09:43.490 --> 09:46.980
But she was still somehow breathing, 
and managed that last desperate yell.

09:46.980 --> 09:49.940
A mother's love for her daughter is grand.

09:49.940 --> 09:52.070
Enough of your bullshit theories!

09:57.450 --> 10:00.450
Did Kaoruko-san check the victim's pulse?

10:01.320 --> 10:03.510
Did she confirm if she was still breathing?

10:03.510 --> 10:07.280
She was wearing gloves so she wouldn't 
leave fingerprints on the knife, wasn't she?

10:07.280 --> 10:10.270
Could she have checked 
her pulse with those on?

10:10.710 --> 10:16.060
<i>This was her plan all along. 
She guided me to the false answer</i>

10:16.060 --> 10:18.580
<i>just so she could corner Uncle Koya.</i>

10:18.580 --> 10:19.590
Well?

10:20.050 --> 10:23.810
Kaoruko told me that she confirmed 
she wasn't breathing anymore!

10:25.830 --> 10:28.210
There were even witnesses 
who said that the body

10:28.210 --> 10:31.020
was still warm when the 
nearby residents found her.

10:31.280 --> 10:33.400
She'd still be warm a few 
minutes after her death!

10:33.400 --> 10:35.980
People don't go cold 
immediately after they die!

10:35.980 --> 10:39.490
But there are many people who 
heard the victim's scream.

10:39.820 --> 10:41.990
Sumi-san was still alive.

10:43.410 --> 10:46.630
Though whether this scream 
came from the love of a mother

10:46.630 --> 10:49.410
or was merely an attempt to protect

10:49.860 --> 10:53.580
the group's image by covering 
for her daughter is unknown.

10:54.660 --> 10:55.410
Now, then...

10:55.410 --> 10:59.240
I'm sure Koya-san is mentally 
exhausted from all my insinuations,

10:59.240 --> 11:00.810
the points I made since yesterday,

11:00.810 --> 11:02.930
and the series of unexpected events.

11:02.930 --> 11:04.560
That could easily make him slip.

11:05.460 --> 11:09.430
This murder occurred 23 years ago. 
There's no evidence left whatsoever.

11:09.830 --> 11:12.800
Unless the suspect mentioned 
something only they'd know,

11:12.800 --> 11:14.520
we'd be stuck in a pointless argument.

11:14.750 --> 11:16.980
Koya-san clearly said a moment ago...

11:17.230 --> 11:21.320
"Kaoruko told me that she confirmed 
she wasn't breathing anymore."

11:26.840 --> 11:27.990
President Otonashi,

11:28.290 --> 11:32.120
the murderer is Kaoruko-san, 
and Koya-san is her accomplice.

11:32.600 --> 11:35.300
But if he was an accomplice 
from the planning stages,

11:35.300 --> 11:40.020
knowing Koya-san's personality, he probably 
wouldn't have let Kaoruko-san, a woman,

11:40.020 --> 11:41.010
carry this out.

11:41.550 --> 11:46.160
That's why I believe Kaoruko-san came up 
with this murder plot and carried it out,

11:46.160 --> 11:49.320
and Koya-san found out about it later.

11:49.890 --> 11:53.190
Perhaps Kaoruko-san was terrified 
of this assignment of yours,

11:53.190 --> 11:57.820
so she finally confessed her crime 
to Koya-san, 23 years later.

11:58.090 --> 12:01.090
That's probably why he 
tried so hard to protect her.

12:01.830 --> 12:03.800
The statute of limitations has already passed,

12:03.800 --> 12:07.170
so all that remains is what you 
and your family believe in.

12:07.480 --> 12:08.870
Please do as you wish.

12:09.250 --> 12:13.170
As I said from the beginning, 
once I leave this hotel,

12:13.170 --> 12:15.410
I'm going to forget 
everything I've heard here.

12:15.900 --> 12:17.000
All I wanted to do

12:17.240 --> 12:22.260
was show that President Otonashi 
relied on powers he never should have.

12:23.150 --> 12:25.840
The president did something 
that goes against order.

12:26.060 --> 12:30.160
And that's why he was destined to 
have to face this truth someday.

12:30.160 --> 12:33.100
If you had tried to kill your
wife with your own hands,

12:33.100 --> 12:36.450
or if you hadn't caved to the temptation 
of doing something illogical,

12:36.450 --> 12:38.110
even if your daughter was the real killer,

12:38.520 --> 12:41.380
you may have believed that your 
wife was killed by a burglar,

12:41.380 --> 12:43.240
and lived out the rest of your life.

12:45.260 --> 12:48.490
Kuro-senpai, let us outsiders 
take our leave now.

12:57.460 --> 12:58.500
Wait.

13:00.250 --> 13:03.540
You really think you can just 
walk out of here now?

13:10.330 --> 13:14.980
<b>Sleeping Murder</b>

13:19.480 --> 13:21.880
Koya-san! Don't do anything rash!

13:21.880 --> 13:24.220
Even if the police find out, 
it won't be a big deal!

13:24.220 --> 13:27.830
None of us are going to speak of this, 
nor are we going to let this get out!

13:27.830 --> 13:32.090
Yes. I believe you, 
the president, and Rion-san,

13:32.090 --> 13:34.030
because you're all part 
of the Otonashi family.

13:34.030 --> 13:36.750
But these two are different.

13:36.750 --> 13:41.040
First off, they had no reason 
to bring the truth to light.

13:41.040 --> 13:45.370
And yet they did, which means 
they must be after something.

13:45.670 --> 13:48.430
No! These two were messed up from the start!

13:49.030 --> 13:50.580
Even if it was an accident,

13:50.580 --> 13:53.570
the effects on the group if this 
gets out will be astronomical!

13:52.040 --> 13:54.560
Uncle... No...

13:53.570 --> 13:57.830
Who knows what these two—
what Iwanaga Kotoko—will do?

13:57.830 --> 14:00.360
We can't let them leave here.

14:00.680 --> 14:02.570
I won't do anything.

14:02.570 --> 14:06.960
You clearly love Kaoruko-san 
and take good care of her.

14:06.960 --> 14:11.070
Kaoruko-san also committed murder 
to have a future with you.

14:11.350 --> 14:13.870
If I were to get in the way 
of such a lovely couple,

14:13.870 --> 14:17.250
the god of love would strike 
me down with divine punishment.

14:17.250 --> 14:21.000
I don't want him messing up my 
relationship with Kuro-senpai, either.

14:21.000 --> 14:25.500
And that's exactly why I have no intention 
of being involved with this any further.

14:26.310 --> 14:30.050
Don't agitate him even more 
by saying stupid things.

14:30.340 --> 14:34.560
Stupid?! I just said I didn't want 
to get involved for personal reasons!

14:35.110 --> 14:40.430
Um... I realize how Iwanaga is, but she 
really doesn't plan on doing anything.

14:40.430 --> 14:42.810
Don't move. This isn't an empty threat.

14:42.810 --> 14:47.820
I admire your courage, but is there 
any reason to protect that girl?

14:47.820 --> 14:52.060
Unfortunately, my life 
can't be bet on anything.

15:11.100 --> 15:15.560
Now there's no turning back for me. 
You and that boy were wrong.

15:15.560 --> 15:20.050
I am correct, and you can still turn back.

15:30.780 --> 15:33.690
I told you, my life can't be bet.

15:34.190 --> 15:35.160
How...

15:35.790 --> 15:39.250
How are you still alive?! 
I shot you right in the head!

15:39.250 --> 15:42.000
The bullet ricocheted and 
embedded itself in the wall!

15:42.000 --> 15:46.960
Um... Oh, you know. It happens 
in period dramas all the time.

15:46.960 --> 15:48.460
When a samurai uses the back of his sword?

15:48.460 --> 15:50.840
How would you even do that with a bullet?!

15:51.130 --> 15:54.260
What happened here is 
basically like a daydream.

15:54.640 --> 15:57.950
Please just think of us as people 
who live in that daydream.

15:57.950 --> 16:00.810
Therefore we aren't tied down 
by the laws or rules of reality,

16:00.810 --> 16:02.150
nor do we care about them.

16:02.520 --> 16:05.520
All right, everyone, we will be 
taking our leave for real now.

16:05.930 --> 16:09.230
I have no intention of making 
the Otonashi Group my enemy.

16:09.490 --> 16:13.370
Do what you think is best, 
President Otonashi. Thank you.

16:24.770 --> 16:26.500
<b>September 18th</b>

16:25.980 --> 16:28.120
<i>Two weeks have passed since all that.</i>

16:28.500 --> 16:32.340
<i>The day after the truth came out 
about the incident 23 years ago,</i>

16:32.620 --> 16:35.340
<i>Aunt Kaoruko tried to take her own life.</i>

16:35.830 --> 16:39.980
<i>She survived because Uncle Koya 
found her early and took action quickly,</i>

16:39.980 --> 16:42.480
<i>but she's been stuck in 
the hospital ever since.</i>

16:42.790 --> 16:45.290
<i>She was terrified that 
this task of Grandfather's</i>

16:45.290 --> 16:48.480
<i>would bring the murder 
she'd committed to light,</i>

16:48.700 --> 16:52.290
<i>so she had been rather 
unstable for about a month.</i>

16:52.920 --> 16:57.490
<i>She couldn't accept the fact that her 
family found out about the murder.</i>

16:57.740 --> 17:01.490
<i>She probably held on to some guilt over 
killing her own mother this whole time.</i>

17:01.810 --> 17:03.460
<i>The shadow was always there.</i>

17:03.820 --> 17:06.070
<i>The incident that took place 23 years ago</i>

17:06.070 --> 17:08.610
<i>did involve a murder and a murderer.</i>

17:08.610 --> 17:10.450
<i>It was just asleep.</i>

17:11.220 --> 17:15.510
<i>If that girl had just withheld the truth, 
that outcome could have been avoided.</i>

17:15.980 --> 17:18.800
<i>But still, she awakened the truth.</i>

17:18.800 --> 17:21.010
<i>And in it was something unknown...</i>

17:21.510 --> 17:25.430
<i>Like Iwanaga Kotoko's own beliefs and rules.</i>

17:25.430 --> 17:28.020
<i>She won't let anything stand in her way.</i>

17:29.220 --> 17:30.460
<i>It's cruel...</i>

17:31.270 --> 17:33.280
<b>Preparing</b>

17:35.530 --> 17:36.690
Uncle...

17:36.690 --> 17:38.740
Hey, I thought I'd stop by.

17:38.740 --> 17:41.160
He came by on his way from the hospital.

17:41.450 --> 17:42.810
Welcome.

17:43.260 --> 17:47.040
<i>The closing of the distance between 
these two may be the only saving grace.</i>

17:47.590 --> 17:51.540
Koya-san is diligently staying 
by Kaoruko-neesan's side.

17:51.970 --> 17:53.850
Dad's worsening, though.

17:53.850 --> 17:57.580
It's probably due to mental fatigue 
on top of dealing with those tumors.

17:57.580 --> 17:59.180
I see...

17:59.540 --> 18:02.680
<i>After all that, Grandfather also 
collapsed and ended up hospitalized.</i>

18:02.910 --> 18:07.700
<i>He wanted to bring his own crime to light 
and exposed Aunt Kaoruko's instead.</i>

18:08.150 --> 18:10.370
<i>He also ended up having to decide</i>

18:10.370 --> 18:14.190
<i>whether or not he wanted to pass 
judgment based on his beliefs.</i>

18:14.440 --> 18:15.950
<i>The cause of all this</i>

18:15.950 --> 18:19.460
<i>could be Grandfather himself, 
as the one who invited that girl.</i>

18:19.460 --> 18:22.450
<i>His self-condemnation is 
whittling down his own life.</i>

18:22.790 --> 18:26.120
Were there no mistakes in 
Iwanaga Kotoko's explanation?

18:26.120 --> 18:30.000
Correct. Back then, Kaoruko-neesan 
married Koya-san,

18:30.000 --> 18:32.620
and to make sure our mother 
didn't crush his business,

18:32.620 --> 18:35.420
she secretly decided to murder our mother,

18:35.650 --> 18:39.160
went through with the plan to falsify 
the time when she broke her leg,

18:39.160 --> 18:42.140
and kept that a secret to Koya-san until now.

18:42.140 --> 18:45.050
The task our father gave us 
reminded her of the past,

18:45.050 --> 18:46.850
and she asked Koya-san for help.

18:46.850 --> 18:49.340
And to think that Koya-san 
actually followed through...

18:50.130 --> 18:55.110
We never should've gotten involved with that 
girl. We don't know anything about her.

18:55.110 --> 18:58.110
Yes. I never want to see her again.

18:59.240 --> 19:02.870
Not that Sakuragawa Kuro guy, either.

19:04.110 --> 19:07.870
I wonder if those two were even human.

19:08.590 --> 19:12.400
I didn't have you come here just 
so I could talk about a grudge.

19:12.400 --> 19:18.700
I brought about that outcome myself,
and it was not outside of my own beliefs.

19:18.700 --> 19:23.140
Just because you didn't show compassion 
and keep the truth to yourselves

19:23.140 --> 19:26.100
doesn't mean I'm going to resent you.

19:26.100 --> 19:28.100
I don't mind listening to some resentment.

19:28.100 --> 19:30.230
I'm not that heartless.

19:30.500 --> 19:34.500
I'm sure you're not at all interested 
in what happened after all that.

19:34.500 --> 19:37.480
Calling you out here goes 
against our promise, as well.

19:37.830 --> 19:41.640
But there was just something 
I wanted to confirm.

19:42.100 --> 19:44.740
Sakuragawa Kuro-kun, wasn't it?

19:44.740 --> 19:48.860
I heard that you're Sakuragawa 
Rikka-san's cousin.

19:50.750 --> 19:53.070
You know Rikka-san?

19:53.410 --> 19:59.470
The first person I talked to about getting 
rid of my guilt was Sakuragawa Rikka-san.

20:00.010 --> 20:05.250
I heard there was some woman who was 
immortal and could see visions of the future,

20:05.250 --> 20:08.010
who'd been in the hospital for a very long time.

20:08.010 --> 20:12.770
It was said that if you talked to 
her, most things would go well.

20:13.000 --> 20:17.230
I don't know the reason she was 
in the hospital for so long.

20:17.230 --> 20:20.030
I had previously made a deal with a yoko,

20:20.030 --> 20:23.640
so I was always interested in 
things that shouldn't exist,

20:23.640 --> 20:26.850
and asked if I could meet her just once.

20:26.850 --> 20:28.280
And...

20:28.280 --> 20:30.790
She was the real deal.

20:31.270 --> 20:36.040
She was beautiful, but she 
seemed clearly inhuman to me.

20:36.040 --> 20:40.300
Around two months ago, 
I coincidentally saw her in town.

20:40.300 --> 20:43.170
I was trying to figure out 
what to do with my past sins,

20:43.170 --> 20:47.050
so I saw this as a message from 
the heavens and talked to her.

20:47.050 --> 20:48.530
She said that if I was troubled

20:48.530 --> 20:51.050
by a problem caused by 
interacting with the supernatural,

20:51.050 --> 20:53.690
I should talk to someone 
involved with the supernatural.

20:54.000 --> 20:57.790
She did seem a bit hesitant, 
but she heard me out.

20:57.790 --> 21:01.340
I didn't tell her about the murder, though.

21:01.340 --> 21:03.670
I told her I had once made 
a deal with a monster,

21:03.670 --> 21:06.910
and asked if she knew of any 
way I could redeem myself,

21:07.260 --> 21:11.290
or if she could use her ability to obtain 
the future that should come to be.

21:11.290 --> 21:14.040
That's what I asked her.

21:14.040 --> 21:15.910
But then, she said...

21:16.790 --> 21:20.580
I have a cousin who possesses 
the same power, and also...

21:21.670 --> 21:26.500
She told me that you two should 
be able to solve my problem.

21:27.700 --> 21:31.450
I wasn't fully convinced, 
but after researching you, Kotoko-san,

21:31.450 --> 21:34.310
so many extraordinary things came up.

21:34.310 --> 21:38.610
And after meeting you, 
I felt an extraordinary power.

21:38.940 --> 21:41.940
You may take offense to my saying this,

21:42.170 --> 21:46.740
but neither of you seem human to me.

21:46.740 --> 21:49.410
That's why I trusted you and 
left this in your hands.

21:49.410 --> 21:51.490
But as I sit here, I wonder...

21:51.490 --> 21:56.490
Why did I ever listen to that Rikka 
woman and decide to trust you?

21:56.870 --> 21:59.380
Now I'm starting to doubt everything.

21:59.380 --> 22:04.620
Could it be that she led me 
to this particular future?

22:07.070 --> 22:11.980
Neither she nor Kuro-senpai is able 
to make just any future come true.

22:11.980 --> 22:15.540
They can only make the most 
probable future come true.

22:15.970 --> 22:18.330
Due to your past experiences,

22:18.330 --> 22:21.090
you were in a mindset where you 
tended to trust the supernatural,

22:21.090 --> 22:25.280
and you strongly wished they 
could take care of this.

22:25.830 --> 22:30.530
Rikka-san probably helped 
relieve some hesitations.

22:30.880 --> 22:34.350
It's not as though she had 
complete control over you.

22:34.700 --> 22:37.540
I see. Yes, you're probably right.

22:38.100 --> 22:41.140
Do you know where Rikka-san is right now?

22:41.140 --> 22:45.170
I haven't seen her since we last parted. 
I didn't ask for her contact info, either.

22:45.170 --> 22:49.180
She probably didn't care 
what the outcome would be.

22:49.180 --> 22:53.660
But perhaps she recommended you two 
because she figured this would happen.

22:53.660 --> 22:54.810
I'm not sure.

22:55.060 --> 22:57.580
She's nothing but a nuisance to me.

22:58.460 --> 23:02.240
To think that Rikka-san was 
the puppet master in this...

23:02.240 --> 23:06.770
I thought it was a bit too convenient 
when the president asked me for help,

23:06.770 --> 23:08.610
but I couldn't read into it any further.

23:08.990 --> 23:11.820
Why did she want me to do this?

23:11.820 --> 23:16.650
Even Rikka-san wouldn't be able 
to understand everything in a case

23:16.650 --> 23:18.510
when she had so little information.

23:18.820 --> 23:21.310
Is she just trying to bully me?

23:21.640 --> 23:24.170
I can think of two reasons.

23:24.680 --> 23:27.590
The first is to have you 
concentrating on this case

23:27.590 --> 23:32.150
so you wouldn't notice 
what she's planning next.

23:32.150 --> 23:34.760
I guess that's much more likely 
than her just bullying me.

23:34.760 --> 23:40.980
The other is to show me how you would 
conclude any problems with the supernatural.

23:41.640 --> 23:45.980
Now? But you've seen that many times.

23:46.300 --> 23:50.920
Yes, but just like this case where 
humans were secretly involved,

23:50.920 --> 23:54.070
she may have thought you'd 
be much more extreme.

23:54.440 --> 23:58.540
This time, you kept your emotions 
out of this to protect order,

23:58.540 --> 24:02.580
and revealed the truth, 
even though tragedy waited in the end.

24:02.940 --> 24:06.250
You show no mercy when it comes 
to order being protected.

24:06.250 --> 24:09.100
Maybe she thought I'd get 
a better look at that.

24:09.100 --> 24:13.220
Wait, wait. Don't make me sound 
like a cruel, emotionless robot.

24:13.220 --> 24:15.700
The one who committed the 
offense is the president,

24:15.700 --> 24:18.390
and there were no emotions 
necessary to set that straight.

24:18.640 --> 24:22.350
Yes, and that's how you should be. 
There's no reason to worry.

24:22.350 --> 24:24.400
Not that you would, anyway.

24:24.400 --> 24:28.900
Your words are what's emotionless here!

24:36.770 --> 24:38.030
Say, Kuro.

24:38.430 --> 24:42.740
You still haven't realized just 
how terrifying Kotoko-san is?

24:57.010 --> 25:00.250
To be continued
